derivations.quote:
Let $A(e)$ bound the operations on a chain from an input to an intermediate coefficient. An invocation has at most $12W$ gates, each taking at most $2W^2$ operations (each output sums at most $W$ terms); inverse-child corrections take at most $4s,$ other corrections $4W+4.$ As $s<Wm,$ the total $24W^3+4s+4W+4$ is below $E=64(W+m+1)^3.$ Chains concatenate the $s$ children; a leaf pair takes eight operations:
$$A(e)\le sA(e/m)+E,\qquad A(e)\le8e\ (	ext{leaf}).$$
With $B=s+E,$ $s\varphi+E\le B\varphi$ for any bound $\varphi\ge1,$ so $A(e)\le8dB^{\lceil\log_mdceil+1}.$ With $
u=\min\{j\ge1:m^j\ge B\},$ $B^{\lceil\log_mdceil+1}\le B^{\log_md+2}=B^2d^{\log_mB}\le B^2d^
u,$ so $A(e)\le8B^2d^{
u+1}.$ The at most $md$ pieces add $8mB^2d^{
u+2},$ individual kernels $8d,$ diagonals and $b^D$ at most $\lfloor D/2floor+9.$ The total is at most $8mB^2d^{
u+2}+18d<128mB^2d^{
u+3}\le\Delta=\lceil C_0d^{C_1}ceil,$ with $C_0=128mB^2,$ $C_1=\max\{20,
u+3\}.$
